$DIR/test.p:8:17: cannot range over c (variable of enum type Color): range over the enum type instead (for v := range Color)
    To loop over the members of an enum, range over the enum type itself, not
    over a value of it.
    Range over the type:
        for c := range Color {
            ...
        }
    (see "For statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.10)
    (run "pluto explain E2317" for a longer explanation)
